WEBVTT

01:07.609 --> 01:11.446
Do you know The Red Shoes
written by Hans Christian Andersen?

01:11.529 --> 01:12.572
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

01:17.827 --> 01:19.287
This happens sometimes when it rains.

01:21.081 --> 01:23.083
I heard everyone was against this hospital

01:23.166 --> 01:25.168
being built where a cemetery used to be.

01:27.921 --> 01:30.673
Maybe it's because earthbound spirits here
are all very resentful.

01:30.757 --> 01:32.801
Be careful
when you do your rounds at night.

01:33.384 --> 01:35.386
I'll let the maintenance team know.

01:41.351 --> 01:42.769
He's fearless.

01:44.813 --> 01:46.731
Yes, the ones in the rooms are fine.

01:47.232 --> 01:49.484
But the lights in the lobby
and the reception area are out.

01:51.611 --> 01:52.695
Yes, okay.

01:53.655 --> 01:55.240
Once you wear those shoes,

01:55.740 --> 01:58.201
your feet start dancing on their own.

01:59.077 --> 02:01.496
And you can never stop dancing

02:02.622 --> 02:05.125
or take off those shoes.

02:07.001 --> 02:11.005
Some things can't be torn apart
no matter how hard you try to do so.

02:28.690 --> 02:29.607
I have

02:30.108 --> 02:33.111
finally found my red shoes.

02:45.456 --> 02:46.583
Why

02:48.126 --> 02:49.294
are you here?

02:49.878 --> 02:50.920
Why do you think?

02:51.838 --> 02:53.423
I came because I missed you.

03:19.741 --> 03:24.954
CHAPTER 3 SLEEPING WITCH

03:34.339 --> 03:36.966
I clearly said I didn't want
to cross paths with you ever again.

03:37.550 --> 03:40.220
You did say that,
but I never agreed to it.

03:49.354 --> 03:50.521
What are you doing?

03:51.522 --> 03:52.815
I'm just fascinated.

03:53.900 --> 03:55.318
You grew up to be a great guy.

03:56.694 --> 03:59.614
I'd say you didn't just grow,
you went through an evolution.

04:03.785 --> 04:04.744
Do you know me?

04:05.828 --> 04:07.288
I want to get to know you better.

04:07.372 --> 04:08.748
When do you get off work?

04:08.831 --> 04:10.625
I rushed here on an empty stomach.

04:10.708 --> 04:12.293
I'm freaking starving right now.

04:12.377 --> 04:14.128
Is there a good restaurant
in this tiny town?

04:16.464 --> 04:17.465
What do you want from me?

04:18.633 --> 04:20.677
I know you won't back off
until you get it,

04:20.760 --> 04:22.512
so tell me what you want.
What do you want?

04:23.263 --> 04:24.597
"Just take it and leave"?

04:24.681 --> 04:26.266
Yes, if you don't mind.

04:27.308 --> 04:28.142
You.

04:29.686 --> 04:30.728
I'll take it and leave.

04:30.812 --> 04:32.981
Moon Gang-tae, what I want is you.

04:36.150 --> 04:38.778
- Why me?
- Because I can't stop wanting you.

04:38.861 --> 04:41.406
- But why?
- Because you're so pretty.

04:43.574 --> 04:46.786
Well, you know.
Like shoes, clothes, and cars.

04:46.869 --> 04:48.579
When I see something pretty, I want it.

04:48.663 --> 04:50.081
And I need to have what I want.

04:50.665 --> 04:52.750
Whether I have to pay for it, steal it,

04:52.875 --> 04:54.127
or just take it by force.

04:54.210 --> 04:55.753
What matters is that I make it mine.

04:55.837 --> 04:58.506
You don't need some grand reason
to desire something, right?

05:08.558 --> 05:09.475
Ms. Ko Mun-yeong.

05:11.936 --> 05:14.981
The director would like to speak
with the patient's guardian.

05:18.693 --> 05:20.069
HOSPITAL MISSION
IT'S OKAY TO NOT BE OKAY

05:20.153 --> 05:23.281
We'll have to see how he recovers,

05:23.698 --> 05:26.200
but his cognitive functions
were impaired to begin with,

05:26.784 --> 05:29.412
so he may not recognize you now
even though you're his daughter.

05:33.207 --> 05:34.792
You can have a seat here.

05:37.086 --> 05:38.129
No, thanks.

05:38.713 --> 05:42.300
Mental disorders accompanied
by brain tumors like your father's case

05:42.383 --> 05:44.177
are difficult to treat.

05:44.427 --> 05:47.346
But we can help reduce the symptoms.

05:47.638 --> 05:48.556
Are you kidding me?

05:48.639 --> 05:51.017
Even if the legendary doctor,
Hua Tuo, is resurrected,

05:51.100 --> 05:52.769
it wouldn't be possible.

05:53.978 --> 05:56.397
His memory is all messed up,

05:56.481 --> 05:58.816
he keeps hearing and seeing things,

05:59.317 --> 06:01.277
and he gets scared for no reason.

06:01.903 --> 06:04.655
Also, he keeps saying things
that make no sense.

06:04.947 --> 06:08.659
His symptoms are really awful, I must say.

06:08.826 --> 06:10.912
Those symptoms remind me
of people who are possessed.

06:11.496 --> 06:12.914
Should I hire an exorcist
and hold a ritual?

06:16.417 --> 06:19.420
I'll write him a prescription
which will be much more effective

06:19.837 --> 06:22.632
than an exorcism or a talisman.

06:40.441 --> 06:42.151
He looks nothing like her, right?

06:43.152 --> 06:44.904
Professor Ko's daughter is very pretty.

06:45.613 --> 06:47.615
I guess she got her looks
from her late mother.

06:48.116 --> 06:49.117
His daughter is here?

06:49.659 --> 06:51.744
Is she pretty?
Which celebrity does she look like?

06:52.620 --> 06:53.704
Did you drink again?

06:54.956 --> 06:56.874
If you keep that up,
you'll be stuck here forever.

06:58.501 --> 06:59.627
No, I didn't drink.

07:00.670 --> 07:03.172
I'm serious. I didn't drink at all.

07:04.465 --> 07:05.716
Here.

07:12.974 --> 07:16.144
OK GROUP THERAPY PROGRAM

07:17.353 --> 07:18.563
What is this?

07:19.188 --> 07:20.815
It's the prescription I just mentioned.

07:21.399 --> 07:25.736
It's our hospital's group therapy program.

07:26.529 --> 07:28.072
Have a look.

07:28.156 --> 07:31.701
From cooking, art, and music
to meditation and gardening,

07:31.784 --> 07:34.370
the program offers all kinds of classes

07:34.454 --> 07:35.705
designed to help treat patients,

07:36.873 --> 07:39.876
except for a class on literature.

07:40.376 --> 07:45.256
In psychiatry, balance is very important.

07:46.215 --> 07:47.091
So what?

07:48.551 --> 07:50.428
Can you help us out for an hour,
twice a week?

07:50.511 --> 07:53.598
It can be about reading or writing.

07:53.681 --> 07:57.560
It doesn't matter. Just think of it as
using your skill sets to do a good deed.

07:58.352 --> 08:00.354
Please teach a class, Ms. Ko.

08:02.064 --> 08:04.317
Well, sir.

08:07.612 --> 08:09.280
The most important part,
the terms and conditions of employment.

08:10.573 --> 08:12.366
Every time you come here to teach,

08:12.450 --> 08:14.869
you can take your father out
for a 30-minute walk.

08:16.370 --> 08:18.789
Shouldn't I be suggesting
the terms that I want?

08:21.292 --> 08:25.671
This is what I prescribe
to the patient and you, his guardian.

08:36.891 --> 08:39.185
I must say, she's got quite a temper.

08:39.477 --> 08:41.854
You didn't actually think
she'd agree to it, did you?

08:42.772 --> 08:45.691
Do you not watch the news?
She's been all over the news.

08:46.400 --> 08:49.028
But she came all the way here
despite what's going on,

08:50.655 --> 08:54.408
which tells me that she's after
someone or something that's here.

09:02.625 --> 09:03.668
Hey, you're here.

09:06.212 --> 09:09.131
Did you see her?
I heard Ko Mun-yeong came by.

09:09.215 --> 09:11.133
Gosh, I heard
she's drop-dead gorgeous in person.

09:11.217 --> 09:12.677
I should've come earlier.

09:13.636 --> 09:16.556
- Do you think she left already?
- Who cares? It's none of your business.

09:17.265 --> 09:18.349
What will you do about this?

09:19.600 --> 09:20.434
What about it?

09:22.353 --> 09:24.021
You botched it all up like this.

09:24.105 --> 09:25.606
You told me to cut it up

09:25.690 --> 09:27.900
because the patients
could hang themselves with it.

09:28.150 --> 09:31.070
I told you to just make a few cuts,
not to cut it into pieces.

09:32.238 --> 09:34.740
Okay, I heard you.
This doesn't even cost much.

09:35.449 --> 09:37.785
I'll just buy a box of it.

09:38.452 --> 09:39.328
You're pissing me off.

09:42.248 --> 09:43.082
Where are you going?

09:44.625 --> 09:45.668
The bathroom.

10:05.062 --> 10:08.024
Just leave it if you're scared
of getting an earful from Ms. Park.

10:08.107 --> 10:09.817
I'll return it later.

10:09.900 --> 10:11.986
Yes, save that for later.
Let's go eat something first.

10:14.488 --> 10:15.448
What are you doing here?

10:28.919 --> 10:30.588
You can't come in here. Get out.

10:30.671 --> 10:33.466
The guy who just left said
I'd find you here and let me in.

10:34.592 --> 10:36.052
- Get out.
- Why?

10:36.135 --> 10:37.637
- Just get out.
- Gosh.

10:43.976 --> 10:45.227
Let go of me.

11:15.424 --> 11:17.593
What? You think we should pretend
not to know each other?

11:18.177 --> 11:19.595
That's what your face is telling me.

11:21.222 --> 11:22.348
I'd appreciate that.

11:23.516 --> 11:24.683
Sure, it's nothing difficult.

11:26.644 --> 11:30.022
How do you and Gang-tae know each other?

11:33.442 --> 11:36.195
Why do you ask? That you can't ignore?

11:37.947 --> 11:39.615
That's something I never understood.

11:40.241 --> 11:45.121
How can you define a relationship
in just one word?

11:54.839 --> 11:57.049
Every encounter we've had
was awfully dramatic,

11:57.133 --> 11:58.384
being an inch away from death.

12:00.094 --> 12:03.514
And every moment we crossed paths,
we surprised each other.

12:16.152 --> 12:18.195
If such coincidences, one after another,

12:18.654 --> 12:20.322
somehow led us here,

12:22.783 --> 12:24.326
how would you define our relationship?

12:28.414 --> 12:30.875
It'd be such a cliché to say
that we're destined for each other.

12:30.958 --> 12:32.084
Right?

12:58.444 --> 12:59.278
Get in.

13:02.406 --> 13:03.282
I said, get in.

13:06.911 --> 13:08.204
Where are you?

13:12.082 --> 13:13.250
I'll call you again later.

13:16.212 --> 13:17.922
Don't waste your energy. Just get in.

13:18.005 --> 13:19.381
Let's go eat some meat. I'm hungry.

13:19.965 --> 13:22.218
Go by yourself. I have plans for dinner.

13:22.301 --> 13:24.220
Oh, with Sang-tae?

13:26.138 --> 13:27.223
That works out perfectly.

13:27.306 --> 13:29.517
We can have the meet-and-greet today.
Where do you live?

13:35.314 --> 13:38.150
I guess bulldozing your way through
like this usually works,

13:38.442 --> 13:39.568
but it'll never work with me.

13:41.695 --> 13:43.739
You're going to play hard to get?

13:44.490 --> 13:45.407
This will be fun.

13:45.491 --> 13:47.326
Let's find out
whether you'll give in or not.

13:49.745 --> 13:50.996
Okay, fine.

13:51.080 --> 13:53.165
Look at those glaring eyes of yours.

13:53.249 --> 13:54.458
I'll leave you alone today.

13:59.380 --> 14:01.882
But I'll kidnap you if you
play hard to get next time I see you!

15:13.662 --> 15:15.789
Fuck, that scared the crap out of me.

15:16.040 --> 15:17.374
Shut up, you stupid deer!

15:18.250 --> 15:19.501
You won't shut up?

15:28.218 --> 15:29.929
SEONGJIN DEER MILK

15:37.353 --> 15:39.730
- Have a great day.
- Thank you.

16:00.542 --> 16:02.378
I thought you were having dinner with her.

16:03.212 --> 16:04.338
No, we're not close.

16:05.881 --> 16:07.675
And dinner is the only meal
I can have at home,

16:08.008 --> 16:09.510
so I should eat with my brother.

16:10.135 --> 16:11.220
Right.

16:15.057 --> 16:16.100
Hey, Jae-su.

16:17.017 --> 16:20.062
I'm in front of the house.
There's Coke in the fridge.

16:20.980 --> 16:22.022
Yes.

16:22.773 --> 16:23.816
Okay.

18:03.582 --> 18:04.416
BORN IN OJI-GUN, SEONGJIN CITY

18:04.500 --> 18:05.876
This isn't good.

18:05.959 --> 18:09.004
Gosh, she really shouldn't go
to this place.

18:10.672 --> 18:11.590
What place?

18:14.802 --> 18:16.053
The cursed castle.

18:36.323 --> 18:38.075
It's a mansion Mun-yeong's father built

18:38.951 --> 18:40.911
to celebrate her birth.

18:42.913 --> 18:45.290
He built it
in the middle of a remote forest

18:47.042 --> 18:49.294
so that his wife could focus
on her writing.

19:30.752 --> 19:34.423
It used to be a fancy mansion, and it even
won a grand award for its architecture.

19:37.593 --> 19:38.927
But it's turned into ruins.

19:39.511 --> 19:40.554
It's like a haunted house.

19:41.889 --> 19:44.308
But she can sell it.
Why hasn't she sold it all this time?

19:44.391 --> 19:47.394
Hey, how can she sell it
when it's not sellable?

19:47.936 --> 19:50.522
Her mother ended up like that
in that house,

19:50.606 --> 19:51.773
and her father...

19:51.857 --> 19:53.567
Even he ended up like this.

19:54.568 --> 19:57.070
Who'd want to buy a house
where so many bad things happened?

19:58.447 --> 19:59.698
"Like that" and "like this"?

20:03.035 --> 20:04.578
What exactly happened to them?

20:04.661 --> 20:07.331
Don't pry, or you'll get in trouble.

20:09.249 --> 20:10.250
Okay.

20:13.045 --> 20:15.672
By the way,
why did Ms. Ko go there out of the blue?

20:16.965 --> 20:17.925
Right?

20:18.508 --> 20:20.427
I wonder why.

20:20.510 --> 20:21.845
What do you think?

20:22.596 --> 20:26.725
It's because some idiot
did a background check on someone

20:26.808 --> 20:29.561
and showed her that
without even telling me!

20:31.939 --> 20:34.566
I did it because I figured it'd be better

20:35.150 --> 20:37.819
than losing my life for not doing the job.

20:37.903 --> 20:39.238
What did you say?

20:39.821 --> 20:41.782
Gosh, you little...

20:42.032 --> 20:44.493
Jeez, seriously. Unbelievable!

22:25.010 --> 22:27.262
Also, he keeps saying things
that make no sense.

22:27.346 --> 22:31.141
His symptoms are really awful, I must say.

22:51.578 --> 22:52.954
I'm hungry.

23:03.173 --> 23:06.843
Grilled pork belly. It looks delicious!

23:13.016 --> 23:14.142
Hey, sweetie.

23:14.226 --> 23:15.310
Open wide.

23:17.354 --> 23:19.648
- Oh, my legs.
- My gosh!

23:19.731 --> 23:21.108
- Take this.
- Here, I got it.

23:21.691 --> 23:23.527
- Gosh, it's hot!
- It's hot. Be careful.

23:23.610 --> 23:24.861
Nice, look at this stew.

23:25.987 --> 23:29.324
This soybean paste stew looks so good!

23:32.744 --> 23:35.956
I was told I'd live a comfortable life
starting at the age of 60.

23:36.039 --> 23:37.541
It was totally right.

23:37.874 --> 23:41.628
Three young men moved into this house
in the middle of nowhere,

23:41.920 --> 23:44.172
and I can even collect rent
every month now.

23:44.840 --> 23:46.758
I live with good people
who bring me money.

23:46.842 --> 23:48.885
I got so lucky in my twilight years.

23:50.470 --> 23:53.807
I'm renting a semi-basement room
that doesn't get much natural light.

23:53.890 --> 23:57.686
It's not fair that I'm paying as much
as they're paying for their rooftop room.

23:58.353 --> 24:00.522
You're renting the biggest room
in this house.

24:04.526 --> 24:06.361
Hey, pass me your bowl.

24:07.445 --> 24:08.488
Sure.

24:10.615 --> 24:11.616
All right.

24:13.827 --> 24:15.036
- Here, have some more.
- My gosh.

24:17.372 --> 24:18.790
That's too much.

24:18.874 --> 24:21.293
I have to take a fistful of pills,

24:21.376 --> 24:23.420
so I need to save some room.

24:26.339 --> 24:28.341
Eat up.

24:28.633 --> 24:30.844
You eat like a bird.
That's why you're so skinny.

24:31.344 --> 24:34.472
Don't force him to eat more.
He won't be able to digest the food.

24:34.556 --> 24:35.432
Goodness.

24:37.475 --> 24:39.769
Look at you.
Didn't you say you were on a diet?

24:46.193 --> 24:47.152
Sang-tae.

24:48.445 --> 24:50.155
Gang-tae has been picked.

24:50.238 --> 24:52.032
What? Someone pinched you?
That must've hurt.

24:52.115 --> 24:53.533
- Where? Your foot?
- No.

24:53.617 --> 24:55.785
I'm saying
she wants him to be her son-in-law.

24:55.869 --> 24:57.037
She's got her eyes on him.

24:57.120 --> 24:59.414
What? The eyes? That's very dangerous.

24:59.497 --> 25:00.832
Hey, eat up.

25:00.916 --> 25:03.752
- Eat. Eat up.
- Eat up.

25:05.629 --> 25:07.047
- Hey, don't.
- Don't do that!

25:07.130 --> 25:08.506
No! A bug!

25:09.424 --> 25:10.550
There's a bug!

25:20.518 --> 25:21.603
It's cold.

25:32.489 --> 25:35.825
Once upon a time
in a castle in the middle of a deep forest

25:37.202 --> 25:40.080
lived a princess
who had been asleep for many years.

26:02.310 --> 26:06.273
"A needle on a spinning wheel
will kill her."

26:07.482 --> 26:09.150
That was the curse

26:09.609 --> 26:13.530
the evil witch put on the princess
the day she was born.

26:14.948 --> 26:17.909
Frightened, the King burned
every spinning wheel in his kingdom

26:17.993 --> 26:19.953
to avoid the curse,

26:20.620 --> 26:24.874
but the princess ended up getting pricked
by a thorn on the rose

26:24.958 --> 26:27.335
given to her by the witch in disguise
and fell asleep.

26:44.311 --> 26:46.313
This fairy tale tells you that

26:46.980 --> 26:50.900
you can never escape your destiny.

26:53.069 --> 26:53.987
Right.

26:55.280 --> 26:56.656
The prince's kiss.

26:57.949 --> 27:01.202
I suppose he could break the curse.

27:04.789 --> 27:06.875
But don't get your hopes up too high.

27:11.338 --> 27:12.464
Because

27:14.591 --> 27:18.136
I will kill that prince.

28:07.811 --> 28:08.937
Save me!

28:10.814 --> 28:11.731
Please...

28:13.400 --> 28:14.776
Save me.

28:18.196 --> 28:19.239
Please...

28:20.156 --> 28:21.366
Save me.

28:25.203 --> 28:26.496
Save me!

28:37.715 --> 28:39.092
When you can't control yourself,

28:40.301 --> 28:42.345
cross your arms like this

28:43.012 --> 28:44.931
and take turns
tapping on each shoulder like this.

29:23.511 --> 29:24.554
Don't cry.

30:27.408 --> 30:28.535
Oh, he's here.

30:33.748 --> 30:34.874
Is he someone high up?

30:35.208 --> 30:37.210
His father is an assemblyman
from this district.

30:39.128 --> 30:40.713
Hey, Min-seok.

30:42.173 --> 30:44.217
- Haeng-ja!
- My gosh.

30:44.300 --> 30:48.221
From afar,
I thought you were Chow Yun Fat.

30:48.304 --> 30:50.557
- How have you been?
- Well, you know. So-so.

30:50.640 --> 30:52.892
Everything's been good
at the hospital, right?

30:52.976 --> 30:54.602
Of course, thanks to you.

30:54.686 --> 30:56.521
- All right, let's go.
- Wait, hang on.

30:56.604 --> 30:59.274
Well, I'm here.

30:59.357 --> 31:01.109
How come the director
is nowhere to be seen?

31:01.192 --> 31:02.986
Oh, is it because of my sunglasses?

31:05.488 --> 31:06.573
Oh, he's in the bathroom?

31:07.156 --> 31:09.450
Yong! Where are you?

31:09.534 --> 31:10.702
Cheo-yong!

31:11.369 --> 31:12.453
Cheo-yong.

31:18.459 --> 31:21.087
I need it to take a nap.
Without it, I'll have sleep paralysis.

31:23.006 --> 31:25.425
All problems can be sorted out.

31:25.967 --> 31:27.635
No, not this.

31:28.386 --> 31:30.013
This one is huge.

31:30.096 --> 31:31.890
There are many witnesses,

31:31.973 --> 31:34.559
and the rumors are spreading so quickly.

31:34.642 --> 31:37.687
Damn it! Why does this country
have to be an IT powerhouse?

31:37.770 --> 31:40.273
Stop whining. You're making my head pound.

31:40.356 --> 31:43.401
Hey, I bet you don't want to cry
as much as I do.

31:43.484 --> 31:46.905
They're even saying you should be
disqualified as a candidate for the award.

31:47.113 --> 31:49.365
And there's an injunction request
against your new book...

31:51.868 --> 31:52.785
Forget it.

31:53.870 --> 31:54.913
Mun-yeong.

31:55.788 --> 31:58.750
Let's just gather some reporters
and cry our eyes out.

31:58.833 --> 32:00.501
I mean, you're a great actress.

32:01.085 --> 32:02.462
I've even written your lines.

32:02.587 --> 32:04.672
"The stress from the creative process,
the new book,

32:04.756 --> 32:07.091
my insomnia, and so on

32:07.175 --> 32:09.636
led me to lose grip over my emotions
and make such a mistake--"

32:09.719 --> 32:10.929
Use Ko Dae-hwan as an excuse.

32:12.096 --> 32:14.349
Who? You mean, your father?

32:14.432 --> 32:15.892
Write this down.

32:15.975 --> 32:17.644
"Ko Mun-yeong disappears.

32:19.604 --> 32:22.231
But turns out, she's been looking after
her father with dementia.

32:22.315 --> 32:23.816
Will she retire from her career?"

32:25.109 --> 32:27.403
End it with a question
so that it sounds like a possibility.

32:29.030 --> 32:30.990
RETIRE

32:33.326 --> 32:34.369
Yes.

32:35.244 --> 32:38.414
The witch disappears
in the middle of a witch hunt.

32:39.749 --> 32:40.750
That's it!

32:41.918 --> 32:43.544
The public will want you back.

32:45.004 --> 32:48.841
Mun-yeong, great minds think alike!

32:48.925 --> 32:51.344
We're such a great team, don't you think?

32:51.928 --> 32:54.097
Hello? Hey, hello?

32:56.557 --> 32:58.476
Goodness, that heartless woman.

32:58.559 --> 33:00.311
You want to use your father as an excuse?

33:02.271 --> 33:03.356
She scares me.

33:13.074 --> 33:14.242
HOW CAN WE HELP?

33:36.305 --> 33:37.640
The show begins now.

33:39.934 --> 33:46.941
IT'S OKAY TO NOT BE OKAY

33:56.409 --> 33:57.827
There's a camera in this room.

33:58.703 --> 33:59.787
I know.

33:59.871 --> 34:03.833
The thought of someone looking at me
intently gets me so excited.

34:06.294 --> 34:07.795
You can put your stuff here.

34:08.796 --> 34:10.256
Why don't you get changed first?

34:10.465 --> 34:11.966
You look very cold now.

34:12.050 --> 34:15.094
No, I'm not cold at all.
You're totally mistaken.

34:16.804 --> 34:18.514
What? Manic syndrome?

34:18.598 --> 34:21.476
He comes here every spring
due to his acute manic episodes,

34:21.559 --> 34:22.977
so make sure he doesn't escape.

34:23.478 --> 34:26.230
Whenever it rains, he sneaks out
and wanders in the mountains.

34:26.314 --> 34:27.607
He's fast, so he's hard to catch.

34:27.690 --> 34:30.735
Gosh, an assemblyman's son
suffers from manic episodes?

34:31.486 --> 34:33.321
Does the President never catch a cold?

34:33.946 --> 34:35.531
Why does his dad's vocation matter?

34:35.615 --> 34:37.825
It's not like his condition
is something he has to hide.

34:39.202 --> 34:41.537
You should not deal with patients
with such biased--

34:41.621 --> 34:44.332
Okay, I heard you.
I will remember that, ma'am.

34:44.415 --> 34:45.917
What? Ma'am?

34:46.000 --> 34:48.419
Hey, I'm not done. Get back here.

34:48.503 --> 34:50.630
Hey, that brat... My gosh, look at him.

34:51.380 --> 34:52.548
Cha-yong.

34:53.132 --> 34:55.760
Hey, that punk...
He must have lost his mind, right?

34:56.385 --> 34:59.889
I'm thinking he might have
oppositional defiant disorder.

35:00.723 --> 35:01.891
Yes.

35:02.767 --> 35:03.935
Well, you're right.

35:04.936 --> 35:06.521
He needs help. I shouldn't be mad at him.

35:07.730 --> 35:09.273
Don't get mad at him, Haeng-ja.

35:09.941 --> 35:11.442
Hey, Cha-yong!

35:13.820 --> 35:16.364
Have you heard of the place called
Morning Sun?

35:17.073 --> 35:20.326
It's a club where you can party
until the sun comes up. Hence the name.

35:20.409 --> 35:22.703
You know, I heard it's the hottest club
at the moment,

35:22.787 --> 35:25.081
so I went there.

35:29.210 --> 35:30.878
The pretty girls and the good music

35:30.962 --> 35:34.799
totally lifted my spirits,
so I did something nice.

35:36.050 --> 35:37.468
All right!

35:38.469 --> 35:41.848
Everything's on me, all night!

35:41.931 --> 35:43.933
- Drink all you want!
- Nice!

35:51.399 --> 35:53.651
I love spending money on others.

35:54.110 --> 35:57.572
I should become a philanthropist
if I have nothing else to do later on.

35:58.030 --> 36:01.659
Anyway, I think the bill came
to about 20 million won that night.

36:01.742 --> 36:02.702
But...

36:05.788 --> 36:07.748
This credit card
has been reported missing.

36:13.629 --> 36:15.548
My dad totally blindsided me.

36:17.049 --> 36:18.509
I had no choice

36:19.302 --> 36:20.595
but to run like fuck.

36:39.780 --> 36:41.782
I just ran into the road
because I had to lose them.

36:41.866 --> 36:44.619
Then I got freaking hot
because I had been running for a while.

36:44.702 --> 36:47.997
And that's why I took off all my clothes!

37:46.013 --> 37:48.182
And I ended up here again.

37:49.433 --> 37:50.810
How fast can you run 100m?

37:51.811 --> 37:53.312
Me? I'm so freaking fast.

37:53.688 --> 37:56.107
See that? About seven seconds, I think.
What about you?

37:56.691 --> 37:58.651
Me? Six seconds.

37:59.402 --> 38:02.321
What? Do you have four legs?
Are you a cheetah or something?

38:02.405 --> 38:03.823
We can have a race if you'd like.

38:06.325 --> 38:07.827
I like you.

38:09.036 --> 38:10.538
Shall we go to the counseling room?

38:11.289 --> 38:12.123
Let's go.

38:12.206 --> 38:13.416
COUNSELING ROOM

38:13.499 --> 38:17.253
My gosh. From the back,
I can tell that you work out.

38:17.336 --> 38:19.630
What do you do? I can tell you're ripped.

38:19.714 --> 38:21.048
- Min-seok!
- Welcome.

38:21.132 --> 38:22.425
Gosh, Min-seok.

38:23.384 --> 38:24.885
You know you have to be here by 3 p.m.

38:26.262 --> 38:27.555
Call me when you get here.

38:28.639 --> 38:31.392
What are you up to now?
Are you doodling on your book again?

38:34.312 --> 38:35.730
No, on the dough.

38:36.772 --> 38:39.358
Jae-su is actually very rich. Who knew?

38:39.442 --> 38:40.609
What?

38:40.693 --> 38:42.695
- Hello.
- Come on in.

38:43.779 --> 38:45.531
Hey, customers. We have customers.

38:45.906 --> 38:48.326
Is it Gang-tae? Hang up.

38:48.409 --> 38:49.577
What was that sound just now?

38:50.036 --> 38:51.120
Hang up. Just hang up!

38:52.246 --> 38:54.040
- Hey, where are you?
- He wants me to hang up.

39:00.588 --> 39:01.422
Gang-tae!

39:02.840 --> 39:04.467
We have to move the patients
to the therapy room.

39:04.550 --> 39:05.509
All right.

39:08.554 --> 39:10.181
By the way, is that really true?

39:10.681 --> 39:13.392
We saw on the sign that a free caricature
comes with a full-size pizza.

39:14.101 --> 39:15.186
Of course.

39:15.269 --> 39:17.313
Just for a month,
to celebrate our grand opening.

39:17.772 --> 39:21.692
Mr. Picasso over there will draw you one
in just ten minutes.

39:23.694 --> 39:24.779
Just a moment, please.

39:25.696 --> 39:28.366
What do I do?

39:28.449 --> 39:29.700
- Sang-tae, they want one.
- Gosh.

39:30.284 --> 39:32.912
If Gang-tae finds out,
we'll get kicked out.

39:32.995 --> 39:35.081
I didn't even go to school
and lied to him.

39:35.164 --> 39:37.917
Gosh, he'll kick me out. No doubt!

39:38.000 --> 39:39.877
Hey, we've already agreed to this.

39:39.960 --> 39:41.504
I'll pay you 10,000 won per caricature.

39:41.587 --> 39:43.798
- You said you needed money.
- Yes, I do need money.

39:43.881 --> 39:45.549
Yes, you can use your skills
and earn money.

39:45.633 --> 39:47.301
The free caricatures
will attract customers.

39:48.010 --> 39:48.928
What's the problem?

39:51.263 --> 39:54.892
Sang-tae, we're doing a good deed.
Consider it a donation.

39:59.438 --> 40:00.689
You're donating your skills.

40:02.858 --> 40:04.151
That is a good deed.

40:05.152 --> 40:06.195
Hello.

40:10.449 --> 40:11.659
THERAPY ROOM

40:25.798 --> 40:28.926
I'm Ko Mun-yeong. I'll be teaching
this literature class from now on.

40:35.766 --> 40:36.767
She's beautiful.

40:40.646 --> 40:43.023
FAIRY...

40:49.738 --> 40:51.699
What is a fairy tale?

40:52.658 --> 40:55.453
The story of me marrying IU.

40:56.203 --> 40:57.455
Stop drinking, will you?

40:57.538 --> 41:00.040
- He's drunk again.
- He's alcohol-dependent, Ms. Ko.

41:00.416 --> 41:02.293
Jeong-tae, you and your drunk talk.

41:02.501 --> 41:04.670
- I'm not drunk.
- I call that bullshit.

41:06.839 --> 41:08.090
Attention, everyone.

41:08.174 --> 41:11.677
A fairy tale is a cruel fantasy
that illustrates

41:11.760 --> 41:16.098
the brutality and violence of this world
in a paradoxical manner.

41:17.975 --> 41:19.059
What?

41:19.560 --> 41:21.479
- A fantasy?
- What did she say?

41:21.562 --> 41:22.980
Shall I give you an example?

41:23.147 --> 41:24.857
What does Heungbu and Nolbu teach us?

41:25.441 --> 41:28.277
If you're a good person,
you'll win the lottery.

41:30.154 --> 41:31.447
- True that.
- Wrong.

41:32.865 --> 41:34.825
Heungbu was poor
because he wasn't the eldest son.

41:34.909 --> 41:36.785
It criticizes the primogeniture customs

41:36.869 --> 41:38.871
that allowed the eldest sons
to inherit everything.

41:39.663 --> 41:41.123
- Is that so?
- Gosh.

41:41.207 --> 41:42.458
What about The Ugly Duckling?

41:43.918 --> 41:46.337
Don't discriminate against ugly kids.

41:46.420 --> 41:49.798
Wrong. The lesson is, "Raising
someone else's child is unrewarding,

41:49.882 --> 41:51.217
so just look after your own."

41:52.134 --> 41:53.719
- Oh, right.
- Excuse me, Ms. Ko?

41:53.802 --> 41:55.137
What about The Little Mermaid?

41:56.138 --> 41:59.141
I know. When you're in love,
you must love that person faithfully

41:59.225 --> 42:02.269
even if that means you'll dissolve
into sea foam.

42:02.645 --> 42:04.480
- My gosh!
- Oh, my!

42:04.563 --> 42:06.815
- My goodness.
- She loved her husband so faithfully

42:06.899 --> 42:09.276
that she let him beat her up to a pulp.

42:10.319 --> 42:11.862
- Ms. Yoo.
- Yes?

42:12.530 --> 42:13.489
That I didn't know.

42:14.323 --> 42:17.952
It wasn't his fault. Alcohol is to blame.

42:21.413 --> 42:22.706
Alcohol is always the problem.

42:26.377 --> 42:27.419
Get out if you want to cry.

42:34.885 --> 42:37.179
All right. The lesson we can take
from The Little Mermaid

42:39.306 --> 42:41.225
is that karma will bite you hard

42:41.308 --> 42:42.977
if you covet an engaged man.

42:44.353 --> 42:47.273
Then what about King Donkey Ears?

42:47.982 --> 42:50.192
Talk behind people's backs
to relieve your stress.

42:52.027 --> 42:54.405
- I see.
- Maybe I should do that.

42:54.488 --> 42:56.156
I guess it kind of makes sense.

42:59.577 --> 43:02.496
So let me sum up today's class for you.

43:03.205 --> 43:06.000
A fairy tale isn't a hallucinogen
that gives us hopes and dreams.

43:06.667 --> 43:08.627
It's a stimulant
that makes us face reality.

43:09.169 --> 43:12.756
So I hope you all read
a lot of fairy tales

43:13.173 --> 43:16.051
and wake up from your dreams.

43:18.345 --> 43:19.555
Ms. Ko.

43:19.638 --> 43:21.599
Don't look up at the stars
in the beautiful night sky.

43:21.682 --> 43:23.642
Look down at your feet
that are stuck in a filthy sewer.

43:24.226 --> 43:27.980
The moment you realize that
and accept your reality...

43:39.283 --> 43:40.117
Let's be happy.

43:40.784 --> 43:42.828
Let's all live happy lives.

43:49.877 --> 43:50.711
Who's here?

43:51.378 --> 43:54.131
I guess you didn't know
because you weren't at the weekly meeting.

43:54.214 --> 43:56.759
The director asked Ms. Ko
to teach literature to our patients

43:56.842 --> 43:59.345
in return for letting her dad
go for a walk every time she visits.

44:00.012 --> 44:02.097
What? "A walk"?

44:03.098 --> 44:05.517
I have to say,
the director really is something.

44:06.143 --> 44:09.104
He said Ms. Ko must have something here
that she wants.

44:09.772 --> 44:11.440
I guess he was right.

44:25.412 --> 44:26.872
How was my first class?

44:28.415 --> 44:29.249
How was it?

44:32.294 --> 44:33.504
Do you really believe that?

44:34.338 --> 44:35.172
What?

44:37.466 --> 44:39.093
That we'll be fine once we accept reality.

44:39.176 --> 44:40.010
Yes.

44:40.094 --> 44:43.138
"This is who I am,
and you are who you are."

44:43.222 --> 44:44.390
We just need to accept that.

44:46.558 --> 44:47.976
So what if we're okay with it

44:48.560 --> 44:50.771
when the entire world
doesn't think that way?

44:51.105 --> 44:52.773
They all refuse to accept...

44:56.110 --> 44:58.028
Sorry. It was so boring
that I almost fell asleep.

45:00.197 --> 45:01.198
Get out so I can turn off the lights.

45:12.334 --> 45:14.670
- Just accept it.
- Accept what?

45:14.878 --> 45:15.921
That you're not satisfied.

45:22.970 --> 45:25.514
See? I can see your eyes
burning with desire.

45:28.600 --> 45:31.311
That's why I like you.
You're arrogant but shallow.

45:34.523 --> 45:36.358
I noticed you're always
smiling to the patients.

45:36.483 --> 45:39.236
But why are you so cold to me?
You were really passionate that night.

45:43.907 --> 45:44.950
What are you talking about?

45:45.868 --> 45:47.619
I dreamt of you a few days ago.

46:06.388 --> 46:08.932
You sat me down on my bed
and did this to me.

46:19.693 --> 46:22.029
Yes, I'm horny. I admit that.

46:22.988 --> 46:24.198
Lower your voice.

46:30.621 --> 46:31.747
Do you want to sleep with me?

46:35.709 --> 46:36.752
What?

46:37.669 --> 46:39.338
She's amazing.

46:42.966 --> 46:44.218
Unbelievable.

46:44.760 --> 46:46.011
UNDER RENOVATION
DO NOT ENTER

46:50.224 --> 46:51.600
I told you to stop.

46:51.975 --> 46:53.477
I'm sick of your jokes.

46:53.560 --> 46:56.104
I have no time to play with you.

46:56.730 --> 46:59.525
That means if you had the time,
you'd play along.

47:01.109 --> 47:02.402
Don't jump to conclusions.

47:02.986 --> 47:04.404
Why live a boring life?

47:06.698 --> 47:08.659
You'll get sick
if you suppress yourself like that.

47:08.742 --> 47:11.537
If you want to have fun, then have fun.
I know you want some fun.

47:14.540 --> 47:15.999
What do you know about me?

47:16.291 --> 47:18.085
Who are you to act up like this?

47:21.588 --> 47:22.548
Hypocrite.

47:37.312 --> 47:38.146
Why are you so startled?

47:38.230 --> 47:40.315
It's not like I called you a murderer.

47:44.027 --> 47:45.237
What's that look on your face?

47:46.029 --> 47:47.531
Someone might think it's true.

47:49.116 --> 47:52.286
People are all hypocrites.
We all live with a lot of hatred,

47:52.369 --> 47:54.246
but we act like that's not the case.

47:59.209 --> 48:01.628
After all, who isn't flawless?

48:25.652 --> 48:28.238
Can you be nicer to A-reum?

48:28.322 --> 48:29.573
What did I do?

48:29.865 --> 48:34.661
Her depression
has gotten worse these days.

48:35.412 --> 48:37.331
Then give her drugs.
There's nothing I can do.

48:49.885 --> 48:52.095
It'll just be a moment.
It'll end even before you know it.

49:07.611 --> 49:08.445
Mr. Ko!

49:09.571 --> 49:10.572
Mr. Ko, what's wrong?

49:14.409 --> 49:15.619
Ms. Ko?

49:16.328 --> 49:18.246
Hey! Let me go!

49:18.455 --> 49:22.209
I'm totally fine! I'm not crazy!

49:22.793 --> 49:23.919
Sang-tae.

49:24.836 --> 49:25.962
Sang-tae.

49:26.630 --> 49:30.050
Gang-tae. Gang-tae won't answer his phone.

49:30.133 --> 49:33.428
I... I pressed number three for emergency.
Number three.

49:33.512 --> 49:34.763
Number three. Nam Ju-ri.

49:34.846 --> 49:37.265
- You did great. Wait here for a moment.
- Okay.

49:41.395 --> 49:43.313
Can you check
Mr. Joo Jeong-tae's test results?

49:43.397 --> 49:44.606
Okay.

49:49.194 --> 49:50.237
Sang-tae.

49:52.280 --> 49:53.281
Sang-tae.

50:06.211 --> 50:07.462
It's Ms. Ko Mun-yeong.

50:09.047 --> 50:10.674
Where did she go?

50:11.717 --> 50:13.427
Did you see Ms. Ko Mun-yeong?

50:24.229 --> 50:25.731
- Sang-tae.
- Ms. Ko Mun-yeong.

50:25.814 --> 50:27.899
What are you doing here?
Ju-ri is looking for you.

50:27.983 --> 50:31.236
Ms. Ko Mun-yeong was here.
I saw Ms. Ko Mun-yeong.

50:31.319 --> 50:33.655
Where did she go? Did you see her?

50:33.739 --> 50:35.532
I bet you were mistaken.
Why would that woman be here?

50:35.615 --> 50:37.242
Not "that woman." Writer Ko Mun-yeong.

50:37.325 --> 50:40.620
Yes, why would Ms. Ko be here?
I'm sure you were mistaken.

50:41.371 --> 50:42.831
- Let's go. You were mistaken.
- Okay.

50:42.914 --> 50:45.667
- You're late.
- I'm sure I saw her here.

50:47.043 --> 50:48.253
Sang-tae, once we get there,

50:49.254 --> 50:51.631
- be polite to the director.
- Okay.

50:53.049 --> 50:54.134
Ms. Ko.

50:55.218 --> 50:56.303
Ms. Ko.

50:58.430 --> 50:59.890
You can't leave already.

50:59.973 --> 51:01.641
You need to take
your father out for a walk.

51:01.725 --> 51:04.060
- Why would I do that?
- What?

51:04.936 --> 51:07.397
I heard that's why you decided
to teach here.

51:07.981 --> 51:09.858
The director told me you made a promise.

51:10.442 --> 51:12.986
That's not true. I don't make promises.

51:17.908 --> 51:18.909
What the...

51:25.040 --> 51:29.377
DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

52:03.245 --> 52:04.663
Stegosaurus.

52:07.082 --> 52:08.875
It has a huge body,

52:08.959 --> 52:10.961
but it has a tiny brain.

52:11.044 --> 52:13.088
It's the dumbest dinosaur
among all dinosaurs.

52:14.130 --> 52:16.675
But it's also very innocent.

52:19.386 --> 52:20.720
What's that guy's name?

52:21.304 --> 52:24.140
Ko Gil-dong. His name is Ko Gil-dong.

52:36.778 --> 52:37.863
Mr. Moon.

52:40.448 --> 52:43.827
This is... This is my favorite book.
This one is my favorite, too.

52:43.910 --> 52:47.122
This is my favorite jelly. The green ones
taste like apple. I love them.

52:47.205 --> 52:49.040
My hat. I wear it when I draw.

52:49.124 --> 52:51.376
I'm not an artist,
but I wear that when I draw.

52:52.127 --> 52:55.005
He gave this to me as a gift.
He seems to like me.

52:57.716 --> 52:59.009
I love them.

53:01.011 --> 53:04.264
Your brother is really good at drawing.

53:04.764 --> 53:07.225
He's too talented
to just keep it as a hobby.

53:07.309 --> 53:08.727
I can even draw your face.

53:08.810 --> 53:11.605
It's 10,000 won per drawing.
You don't need to order pizza.

53:16.526 --> 53:19.571
By any chance, did he mention
anything about butterflies?

53:20.155 --> 53:21.364
"Butterflies"?

53:22.365 --> 53:23.325
No.

53:24.701 --> 53:26.745
Today's his first day.
I'm sure he'll tell me one day.

53:33.585 --> 53:34.961
- Sang-tae.
- Yes?

53:35.462 --> 53:38.298
Isn't the outside view beautiful?

53:38.381 --> 53:40.508
It's the best thing about our hospital.

53:41.509 --> 53:45.472
But you see, I'd like to move that view
to somewhere else.

53:45.555 --> 53:47.724
- Will you help me do that, Sang-tae?
- Yes.

53:54.189 --> 53:56.816
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

53:57.859 --> 53:59.277
Move it to where?

54:01.821 --> 54:03.114
I want to move it here.

54:04.366 --> 54:05.659
Sang-tae,

54:06.326 --> 54:08.536
I bet you're talented enough to draw

54:08.954 --> 54:11.706
the exact picturesque view
from my office window.

54:13.875 --> 54:15.126
Can you do it?

54:15.919 --> 54:17.295
But sir--

54:17.379 --> 54:20.215
This is my prescription for him.

54:21.132 --> 54:22.509
How much

54:24.469 --> 54:25.637
are you going to pay?

54:26.221 --> 54:28.014
How much... How much money will you pay?

54:29.182 --> 54:30.684
- How much will I get paid?
- What?

54:30.767 --> 54:33.269
- Sang-tae--
- I'll do it if you pay me a lot.

54:33.353 --> 54:35.021
How much are you going to pay me?

54:39.442 --> 54:40.777
That depends on your drawing.

54:44.531 --> 54:45.615
Sang-tae.

54:46.366 --> 54:48.118
How much will I get paid?

54:56.710 --> 54:57.877
Let's see.

55:09.431 --> 55:10.348
Sang-tae, you're rich.

55:12.308 --> 55:13.810
Let me see. How much did you save up?

55:13.893 --> 55:17.939
No, no. I won't...
I won't show this to anyone

55:18.023 --> 55:19.607
until I reach my goal.

55:22.110 --> 55:23.111
But I'm your brother.

55:23.194 --> 55:25.947
To an autistic person,
family members are like close strangers.

55:26.031 --> 55:27.532
A close stranger.

55:32.162 --> 55:33.830
So how much do you plan to save up?

55:33.913 --> 55:36.416
I need 32,890,000 won.

55:37.375 --> 55:39.544
- What are you going to buy with that?
- I will buy a car.

55:40.170 --> 55:41.504
- A car?
- A car.

55:42.672 --> 55:43.673
Why all of a sudden?

55:44.883 --> 55:46.009
A car.

55:48.386 --> 55:50.764
- Is that also a secret?
- A car.

55:54.684 --> 55:55.810
Okay, I won't ask.

56:11.618 --> 56:15.080
WALK-THROUGH VAN CAMPING CAR
32,890,000 WON, WE'RE HAVING A HUGE SALE

56:15.955 --> 56:18.833
"It will give you good memories
and a romantic lifestyle.

56:18.917 --> 56:21.169
Wherever you go,
it will always feel comfortable like home.

56:22.921 --> 56:26.966
It costs 32,890,000 won. We're having
a huge sale." A... A huge sale.

56:27.050 --> 56:28.218
It's really cheap.

56:29.886 --> 56:31.221
Why do you want this?

56:31.721 --> 56:34.682
If we buy that,
we won't have to move every year.

56:34.766 --> 56:36.976
We can run away
even if the butterfly chases us.

56:37.393 --> 56:40.063
We don't need to pack up
and move somewhere else.

56:40.146 --> 56:43.983
Then... Then the landlord
won't get angry at my brother.

56:44.067 --> 56:45.944
We can go anywhere.

56:50.865 --> 56:51.783
Sang-tae.

56:52.575 --> 56:56.496
I still need 32,270,000 won more.

56:58.540 --> 56:59.707
Sang-tae.

57:01.459 --> 57:04.629
I don't need a house, car, or money.

57:06.214 --> 57:07.590
All I need is you.

57:07.674 --> 57:08.591
Hypocrite.

57:10.760 --> 57:11.928
I mean it.

57:12.595 --> 57:13.847
You're my everything.

57:15.974 --> 57:18.476
It's really hard to make money, you know.

57:23.731 --> 57:26.151
I need 32,890,000 won.

57:26.776 --> 57:28.987
I need three thousand and...

57:33.324 --> 57:36.619
OK PSYCHIATRIC HOSPITAL

57:36.703 --> 57:38.538
I will get rid of OK Psychiatric Hospital

57:38.621 --> 57:41.332
- and the juvenile hall that has been
- All the politicians

57:41.416 --> 57:44.252
- making our residents feel unsafe.
- try so hard to get rid of our hospital

57:44.335 --> 57:46.254
every time they get ready for an election.

57:46.337 --> 57:49.174
But still, his own son gets treated here.

57:49.257 --> 57:50.508
How could he do that as his dad?

57:51.134 --> 57:53.636
He cares more about his job
than his own son.

58:04.981 --> 58:05.940
Seagull 777.

58:06.024 --> 58:07.650
- I repeat. Seagull 777.
- Stop!

58:07.984 --> 58:09.360
Get away from me!

58:09.444 --> 58:12.030
- Back off! Go away!
- No, stop!

58:13.573 --> 58:15.366
Sorry! Just a moment!

58:15.450 --> 58:17.869
- Mr. Kwon, stop!
- Oh, gosh!

58:34.886 --> 58:36.012
Oh, my goodness.

58:39.307 --> 58:41.559
I can hear your heart beating.

58:43.186 --> 58:44.437
See you.

58:47.440 --> 58:48.441
Mr. Kwon.

58:51.402 --> 58:52.237
Hey!

58:56.950 --> 58:59.244
I told them they're not allowed
to run inside the hospital.

59:03.498 --> 59:05.500
MIGHWAY, ENGLAND,
16,500,000 WON

59:06.834 --> 59:08.545
DETAILED INFORMATION
PRICE: 16,500,000 WON

59:12.924 --> 59:14.300
Are you planning to go camping?

59:15.260 --> 59:16.386
No, I'm just looking.

59:18.388 --> 59:20.765
One of my friends
rents out camping cars for a living.

59:20.848 --> 59:23.685
We should rent one
and go on a trip together.

59:30.900 --> 59:32.902
Let's go when we get the same off day.

59:34.737 --> 59:37.574
Then I'll check next month's schedule
and...

59:38.992 --> 59:39.826
Hey.

59:40.618 --> 59:41.452
What? He escaped?

59:42.829 --> 59:43.997
When?

59:45.331 --> 59:46.165
Next.

59:46.833 --> 59:49.669
He started free voiding
and wet himself during consultation.

59:49.752 --> 59:51.087
So I went to get a new gown and...

59:51.879 --> 59:53.965
- Where did he go?
- Well...

59:54.465 --> 59:56.050
Hey, wait.

59:56.134 --> 59:58.011
Isn't that Ms. Ko Mun-yeong's car?

59:58.094 --> 01:00:00.597
- Yes, I think so.
- I think you're right.

01:00:28.207 --> 01:00:31.794
Is this what people would call
a "teeny-weeny weenie"?

01:00:32.962 --> 01:00:33.963
Because it's tiny?

01:00:37.842 --> 01:00:41.512
It's... It's cold. That's why it's...

01:00:44.724 --> 01:00:46.100
He must be on his way to work.

01:00:46.225 --> 01:00:47.644
Great timing. Get in.

01:00:48.561 --> 01:00:49.437
What?

01:00:49.520 --> 01:00:51.356
- Get in.
- Okay.

01:00:59.489 --> 01:01:03.117
I'm not intimidated or anything,
but let me wear my underwear.

01:01:03.201 --> 01:01:04.577
You carry around your underwear?

01:01:04.661 --> 01:01:06.537
No, don't think of this as my underwear.

01:01:06.621 --> 01:01:09.540
It's the only thing
that prevents me from losing my mind.

01:01:10.833 --> 01:01:12.919
Ko Mun-yeong kidnapped him.

01:01:23.763 --> 01:01:26.015
Drive faster! Go!

01:01:38.569 --> 01:01:39.445
Ju-ri, stop the car.

01:01:49.539 --> 01:01:50.623
Ko Mun-yeong!

01:01:51.332 --> 01:01:53.292
- Stop the car!
- Gang-tae, move! It's dangerous!

01:01:54.419 --> 01:01:55.503
There he is.

01:01:57.380 --> 01:01:58.589
It's that handsome guy!

01:01:58.673 --> 01:02:01.217
Is he here for me? My gosh!

01:02:01.300 --> 01:02:03.010
- Gang-tae!
- Don't come!

01:02:04.512 --> 01:02:06.222
- Stay right there.
- Hey, wait...

01:02:06.973 --> 01:02:10.435
There's... There's someone there.

01:02:12.812 --> 01:02:14.272
Hey, stop.

01:02:22.780 --> 01:02:23.781
Wait!

01:02:47.221 --> 01:02:49.265
Do you still like me?

01:02:58.441 --> 01:03:00.443
- Coward.
- "Hope I never see you again."

01:03:01.110 --> 01:03:03.237
Please. Let's not meet again.

01:03:03.321 --> 01:03:05.740
You're different from patients.

01:03:06.365 --> 01:03:08.284
It's just best to avoid people like you.

01:03:23.216 --> 01:03:26.093
It's a urinating disorder. It's common
among people who suffer from manic--

01:03:26.177 --> 01:03:27.220
Shut your mouth.

01:03:30.598 --> 01:03:32.016
That crazy bitch.

01:03:32.683 --> 01:03:33.810
Get out of the car.

01:03:37.188 --> 01:03:38.356
You're not running away.

01:03:39.774 --> 01:03:41.776
You're not avoiding me either.
I'm impressed.

01:03:43.152 --> 01:03:45.279
- Get out of the car.
- He wants you out of the car.

01:03:45.863 --> 01:03:48.115
No! I don't want to go!
I want to go and have fun!

01:03:48.282 --> 01:03:50.493
Just get in the car.
Let's go have fun together.

01:03:50.576 --> 01:03:52.495
Get out of the car right now!

01:03:57.208 --> 01:03:58.417
Why are you always

01:03:58.501 --> 01:03:59.836
so angry at me?

01:03:59.919 --> 01:04:01.379
Because...

01:04:03.506 --> 01:04:04.799
you make me get angry.

01:04:06.217 --> 01:04:07.635
Why not just ignore me?

01:04:07.885 --> 01:04:09.053
But you know what?

01:04:09.762 --> 01:04:11.848
You should always be careful

01:04:13.266 --> 01:04:14.350
not to be off guard.

01:04:19.730 --> 01:04:20.731
Let me borrow your car!

01:04:27.363 --> 01:04:28.489
Be careful!

01:04:49.010 --> 01:04:51.220
He keeps following us!

01:04:56.475 --> 01:04:58.519
Drive faster! He's getting near us!

01:05:02.231 --> 01:05:04.066
Hey! Hey, dude!

01:05:07.570 --> 01:05:09.030
Pull over!

01:05:09.614 --> 01:05:10.781
Pull over right now!

01:05:11.365 --> 01:05:12.575
I don't want to.

01:05:24.086 --> 01:05:26.672
- Vote for number one, Kwon Man-su!
- Vote for number one, Kwon Man-su!

01:05:29.008 --> 01:05:30.801
- Vote for Kwon Man-su!
- Vote for Kwon Man-su!

01:05:32.511 --> 01:05:33.554
Hello!

01:05:33.638 --> 01:05:35.514
- Vote for Kwon Man-su!
- Vote for Kwon Man-su!

01:05:38.976 --> 01:05:40.561
Listen up, residents of Seongjin City!

01:05:40.686 --> 01:05:43.064
Don't vote for candidate number one,
Kwon Man-su!

01:05:43.356 --> 01:05:46.400
He's a complete hypocrite,
and he discriminates people!

01:05:46.484 --> 01:05:49.904
I know him best
because I'm his youngest son!

01:05:52.365 --> 01:05:53.282
Don't vote for him!

01:05:53.366 --> 01:05:55.660
Don't vote for him!
Don't vote for Kwon Man-su!

01:05:56.285 --> 01:05:59.038
Number 7040. 7040. Stop the car.

01:06:00.164 --> 01:06:01.999
Number 7040. Pull over.

01:06:05.878 --> 01:06:07.463
Stop the car right now! Number 7040!

01:06:12.510 --> 01:06:13.928
Stop the car!

01:06:16.514 --> 01:06:17.848
Number 7040. Pull over.

01:06:27.149 --> 01:06:29.068
Get out of the way! Move!

01:06:39.370 --> 01:06:41.872
Oh my gosh!

01:06:46.711 --> 01:06:48.713
That's a lot of chili peppers.

01:06:55.094 --> 01:06:56.220
Oh, my goodness!

01:07:08.274 --> 01:07:10.317
- Watch out for the bang!
- Watch out for the bang!

01:07:25.291 --> 01:07:26.751
KWON MAN-SU'S ELECTION CAMPAIGN

01:07:26.834 --> 01:07:27.877
My goodness, thank you.

01:07:27.960 --> 01:07:30.421
- Is everyone doing well?
- Yes, it's all thanks to you.

01:07:30.504 --> 01:07:31.756
My goodness.

01:07:31.839 --> 01:07:34.467
His favorite food is mung-bean pancakes.

01:07:34.550 --> 01:07:35.760
Here.

01:07:35.843 --> 01:07:37.344
My goodness, you're so kind.

01:07:48.189 --> 01:07:49.190
Hey, Teeny-weeny.

01:07:51.192 --> 01:07:52.485
Let's have fun here.

01:08:00.409 --> 01:08:01.952
- I'm Kwon Man-su.
- Thank you.

01:08:02.036 --> 01:08:03.454
- Here.
- Thank you.

01:08:03.537 --> 01:08:04.538
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.

01:08:05.164 --> 01:08:07.416
- Please vote for number one.
- Of course.

01:08:07.750 --> 01:08:09.168
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

01:08:09.251 --> 01:08:10.586
- Thank you in advance.
- Thank you.

01:08:10.669 --> 01:08:11.754
- No problem.
- Thank you.

01:08:11.837 --> 01:08:12.963
- Enjoy.
- Goodbye.

01:08:13.506 --> 01:08:14.715
Hello, everyone!

01:08:15.841 --> 01:08:17.343
I'm Kwon Man-su's youngest son!

01:08:17.426 --> 01:08:18.761
My name is Kwon Gi-do!

01:08:18.886 --> 01:08:20.596
What... What the hell is he doing there?

01:08:20.679 --> 01:08:22.431
As you can see, I'm mentally ill!

01:08:22.515 --> 01:08:23.974
What is that punk doing there?

01:08:24.558 --> 01:08:28.062
Yes, that's right.
I'm the ugly duckling of the family.

01:08:30.106 --> 01:08:31.357
- Sir.
- My goodness.

01:08:31.440 --> 01:08:33.442
- My goodness.
- I'm the embarrassment of our family!

01:08:35.778 --> 01:08:36.862
Hello?

01:08:36.946 --> 01:08:38.697
I'm calling from the park
in Seongjin City.

01:08:47.373 --> 01:08:49.667
You see, everyone in my family

01:08:50.000 --> 01:08:53.671
including my parents, siblings,
and my cousins

01:08:53.754 --> 01:08:56.841
went to Seoul National University
School of Law.

01:08:57.508 --> 01:09:00.678
I was the only stupid one in my family.

01:09:03.681 --> 01:09:06.016
But that's not my fault.

01:09:08.060 --> 01:09:09.103
I was...

01:09:10.813 --> 01:09:13.607
I was just born a little dumb.

01:09:18.779 --> 01:09:20.781
But he hit me
because I didn't get good grades.

01:09:22.616 --> 01:09:24.952
He looked down on me
because I couldn't understand properly.

01:09:25.411 --> 01:09:27.037
He locked me up for causing trouble.

01:09:36.172 --> 01:09:38.299
I mean, I'm also his child.

01:09:41.760 --> 01:09:43.345
But he treated me like I was invisible.

01:09:43.429 --> 01:09:44.638
I just...

01:09:51.228 --> 01:09:53.647
I just wanted his attention, you see.

01:09:57.735 --> 01:09:59.361
I just wanted him to look at me.

01:10:01.155 --> 01:10:03.073
So I did tons of crazy stuff
to get his attention.

01:10:05.075 --> 01:10:09.079
I just ended up going crazy!

01:10:29.266 --> 01:10:32.811
Look at me, look at me

01:10:32.895 --> 01:10:36.148
Look at me

01:10:36.232 --> 01:10:39.652
Take a look at number one
Kwon Man-su's son

01:10:39.777 --> 01:10:42.321
Kwon Gi-do

01:11:33.872 --> 01:11:36.041
He's having so much fun.

01:11:40.754 --> 01:11:41.839
Don't you agree?

01:11:44.967 --> 01:11:46.176
Should I just

01:11:48.345 --> 01:11:49.513
have fun with you?

01:11:58.522 --> 01:11:59.565
Should I do that?

01:12:11.243 --> 01:12:13.203
Look at me

01:12:13.287 --> 01:12:16.332
Look at me

01:12:16.415 --> 01:12:19.752
Take a look at number one
Kwon Man-su's son

01:13:04.129 --> 01:13:06.673
Have you heard of the place called
Morning Sun?

01:13:07.966 --> 01:13:10.969
It's a club where you can party
until the sun comes up. Hence the name.

01:13:11.053 --> 01:13:13.597
You know, I heard it's the hottest club
at the moment,

01:13:13.680 --> 01:13:15.557
so I went there.

01:13:15.641 --> 01:13:17.351
DO NOT DISTURB

01:13:21.980 --> 01:13:24.233
The pretty girls and the good music

01:13:24.316 --> 01:13:26.443
totally lifted my spirits,

01:13:26.527 --> 01:13:28.570
so I thought I should do something nice.

01:13:28.654 --> 01:13:30.531
Everything's on me, all night!

01:13:30.614 --> 01:13:32.991
- Eat up! Drink all you want!
- Nice!

01:13:36.203 --> 01:13:37.413
You're the best!

01:13:38.372 --> 01:13:41.333
I love spending money on others.

01:13:41.417 --> 01:13:44.586
Anyway, I think the bill came
to about 20 million won that night.

01:13:49.007 --> 01:13:50.509
This credit card
has been reported missing.

01:13:50.592 --> 01:13:51.927
What?

01:13:52.553 --> 01:13:54.263
My dad totally blindsided me.

01:13:54.346 --> 01:13:57.391
I had no choice but to run like fuck.

01:13:59.268 --> 01:14:00.644
You're too kind.

01:14:02.354 --> 01:14:03.522
Don't take your eyes off him.

01:14:04.940 --> 01:14:07.734
I just ran into the road
because I had to lose them.

01:14:07.943 --> 01:14:10.404
Then I got freaking hot
because I had been running for a while.

01:14:10.487 --> 01:14:13.115
And that's why I took off all my clothes!

01:14:31.592 --> 01:14:33.093
And I ended up

01:14:37.973 --> 01:14:39.266
here again.

01:15:12.758 --> 01:15:14.051
Does a child

01:15:15.093 --> 01:15:17.387
- need to be of any use to a parent?
- Why did you do that?

01:15:17.554 --> 01:15:18.931
- You little...
- Why did you do that?

01:15:20.682 --> 01:15:22.184
I can see that

01:15:23.393 --> 01:15:24.353
you want to be loved.

01:15:25.896 --> 01:15:27.689
Girls like funny guys.

01:15:30.108 --> 01:15:32.528
I warned you to stay away from my brother.

01:15:32.694 --> 01:15:34.279
Are you still mad at me?

01:15:34.738 --> 01:15:35.781
Don't be delusional.

01:15:36.198 --> 01:15:38.492
Until the day you die...

01:15:38.575 --> 01:15:40.452
Until the day you die...

01:15:40.953 --> 01:15:42.538
You won't understand me.

01:15:49.336 --> 01:15:51.380
Subtitle translation by Ja-won Lee
